      "side": 1,
      "message": "Closing the thread as the CL doesn\u0027t have the initial issue anymore.\n\nquick brainstorming:\n\n\u003e translating them from \"bluetooth\" formats to \"Android\" formats\n\nThis should be an instant operation in my opinion so fine on the shared thread\n\n\u003e calling functions to insert/update the data at rest\n\nDo you mean database write ? Then yes, the database should have an async i/o in order to not block accessor, but that mean that various profiles could get rid of they own thread (or at least rid of the \"one thread per device\" architecture).\n\n\u003e I think we can leverage things like quit()/quitNow()\n\nYep, that\u0027s [what you do](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Bluetooth/android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/mapclient/MceStateMachine.java;l\u003d271;drc\u003db4d6320e2ae398b36f0aaafb2ecd83609d2d99af)\n---\n\nAlso, is this frequent to have more than one PBAP / MAP client at the same time ? I would assume that there is only one phone connected at a time to the car, but I don\u0027t know the usecase here.",
